{
  "tool": "ecosystems",
  "owner": "FIT Site",
  "version": "2026-10-18",
  "tolerance": {
    "rel": 1e-06,
    "abs_when_expected_zero": 1e-09,
    "note": "numbers relative 1e-6 (7 s.f.), zero absolute 1e-9; integers, booleans, strings, nulls, lists, name-keyed objects and error objects exact; errors {error: schema class, reason: lower_snake_case} (KAT_SCHEMA 17:46)"
  },
  "calc_module": "lib/sims/families/ecosystems.calc.js",
  "convention": "Module FITCalcEco (lib/sims/families/ecosystems.calc.js); op = function name, fields exactly as the family prompt. Food web: eats = [[predator, prey], ...]; energy flows prey -> predator; producers eat nothing, top consumers are eaten by nothing (both listed in the order of organisms); chain_count = number of distinct producer-to-top-consumer chains; longest_chain = most organisms in one chain; max_trophic_level = 1 + the longest chain below it (producers 1); cycles, self-links, unknown or unlinked organisms are ConstraintViolations. remove_effect is first-order only: prey of the removed organism increase, its predators decrease, all others unchanged; starving = predators whose only food was the removed organism. Pyramid shape: 'upright' if non-increasing up the levels, 'inverted' if non-decreasing (and not upright), else 'irregular'. exponential N0 e^(rt), doubling ln2/r (null if r <= 0). logistic N = K/(1 + ((K-N0)/N0) e^(-rt)), N0 = 0 stays 0; logistic_time reaches N_target in finite positive time or MathError target_not_reachable (K itself, wrong side, N0 = 0). harvest: constant-quota logistic, MSY = rK/4, equilibria ascending; |h - MSY| <= 1e-9 max(1, MSY) is at_msy. quadrat: density = mean count / quadrat area; percent_frequency = % of quadrats with at least one. Simpson D = sum n(n-1)/(N(N-1)), simpson_diversity = 1 - D; Shannon natural log; evenness H/ln S (null if S < 2). Lotka-Volterra: dx/dt = alpha x (1 - x/K) - beta x y (K null: no 1 - x/K term), dy/dt = delta x y - gamma y; lv_simulate classical RK4, fixed dt, extremes over all steps + 1 recorded points including the start; lv_period = 2 pi / sqrt(alpha gamma) (small oscillations); lv_invariant H = delta x - gamma ln x + beta y - alpha ln y.",
  "oracle": "script-verified textbook formulae (Singapore school biology; Begon, Townsend and Harper, Ecology; Murray, Mathematical Biology; Krebs, Ecological Methodology). Builder = memoised DFS, closed forms, classical RK4; check() = adjacency-matrix powers + Kahn sort + relaxation, scipy solve_ivp DOP853 (rtol 1e-12) with events, brentq, fsolve, numpy.roots, Jacobian eigenvalues, scipy.stats.entropy, exact Fractions, and quad integrals for the invariant.",
